\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Let $N$ be RSA-1024, the following fixed integer. Its decimal digits are obtained by concatenating the displayed lines in order:
\[\begin{gathered}
1350664108659952233496032162788059699388814756\\
0566702752448514385152651060485953383394028715\\
0571909441798207282164471551373680419703964191\\
7430464965892742562393410208643832021103729587\\
2576235850964311056407350150818751067659462920\\
5563685529475213500852879416377328533906109750\\
544334999811150056977236890927563
\end{gathered}\]
A prime factorization is an expression $N=\prod_{j=1}^{t}q_j^{e_j}$ with distinct primes $q_j$ and positive integer exponents $e_j$.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Find the prime factorization of this exact 309-digit integer $N$. \href{https://unsolvedproblems.org/index_files/RSA.htm}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Factor the fixed RSA-1024 challenge number, rather than solve a general factoring problem.

